# This governs the BACKEND image only — ./Dockerfile, built from the repository
# root because it needs data/. The website builds from frontend/ as its own context
# and has its own frontend/.dockerignore.
#
# What this list is for: keeping a multi-hundred-megabyte context off the wire and,
# more importantly, keeping a local .env out of an image.

.git
.github

# ---- secrets: never in an image, regardless of .gitignore ----
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
secrets/
service-account*.json
credentials*.json

# ---- Python ----
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv
**/venv
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/*.egg-info
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov

# ---- Node ----
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/out
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/npm-debug.log*

# ---- Large artefacts nothing in a running container reads ----
docs/screenshots
frontend
# The serving image (./Dockerfile) does not COPY the harness — nothing in
# backend/app reads it — but the evaluation delivery worker (evals/Dockerfile)
# does, so `evals` stays in the shared root context rather than being excluded
# here. The website renders the committed copy at
# frontend/src/data/evaluation-report.json, which CI checks against
# evals/reports/latest.json.
